{"title":"2004 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A floor with an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/c/bcce78db89b0b83cf88d2812da6d3d4d84cc9476.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\text{ m}^2$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> will be covered by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> rugs with various shapes, each having an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/a/d5a4d00251092ed3a1756a1f9db03dc5c05bb388.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\text{ m}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" />. Show that there exist <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> overlapping rugs with the overlapped area at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/6/476d47d82d0b04a28c9d66544fa4fce2f72a32b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/5 \\text{ m}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the first 3 rugs occupy the entire floor, then the next rug that you add in, by the pigeon hole principle, it must overlap with another rug. Let a, b and c be the overlapping region with rug 1, rug 2 and rug 3 respectively, a+b+c = 1, thus at least one of a, b and c must be greater than 0.2.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that a, b, c, d, e are the area each rag covers. Then, by principle of inclusion-exclusion, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/d/a2df9ead35f855db2f2adc34ed51efb13b6b154e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b+c+d+e) - (a\\cap b + a\\cap c + a\\cap d + a\\cap e + b\\cap c + b\\cap d + b\\cap e + c\\cap d + c\\cap e + d\\cap e)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"759\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7ce11408b1fb5fb1897ead716a141b5a43d75b3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+(a\\cap b\\cap c + ...+c\\cap d\\cap e) - (a\\cap b\\cap c\\cap d + ...+ b\\cap c\\cap d\\cap e)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"507\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/2/b722356043622cf84f6becef26a0226865957b98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+(a\\cap b\\cap c\\cap d\\cap e) = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"187\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Let p, q, r, s indicate the area overlapped by at least 2 rags, 3 rags, 4 rags, and 5 rags, respectively, then the above equation can be replaced as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/3/273e914cb2bf5a60765e1029935040dadde97d1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+p-q+r-s=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"168\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><br />\nWe will use contradiction\n</p><p><br />\nSuppose it is indeed possible for an arrangement such that each overlap of 2 or more rags covers less than 0.2 area and the total covered area is equal to 3.\n</p><p>Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/5/52517e9b8a9d773dba14fd7c7426d04bfbbf8dba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le s &lt; 0.2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Since r represents the sum of 5 intersecting rags, with each overlapped area &lt; 0.2, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/2/df2c7fb0a4774faf1ba21a126fb9d6e1dc46bf74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\le r &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/2/7921c0d5e08fc720432e777d78132ef3cfd75124.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r\\le q &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" />, since q is the sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/0/fc07a18c4d98829a5b79e17cc961c0d5a8168610.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${5 \\choose 3} = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"79\" height=\"53\" /> overlapped area, where each area &lt; 0.2.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/a/5eada2b9702fde999233662adcd32f0964770bf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q\\le p &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" />, since p is the sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/c/d6c94958d0979e8c92439a3dd2ec9779a37ab470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${5\\choose 2} = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"79\" height=\"53\" /> areas.\n</p><p>From the restrictions, we know that the total area = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0a27d33eb48c0db05130591af6b15b66324ea12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5-p+q-r+s \\ge 5-p+r-r+s &gt; 5-2+s = 3+s \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"485\" height=\"17\" />. Thus, Total Covered Area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/c/60c9e77a789e468d14094d0f0633b29dfd8be425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 5-p+q-r+s &gt; 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"187\" height=\"17\" />, which is a contradiction.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017203933\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.021 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 69/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3308/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:18440:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017203933 and revision id 227140. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}